<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bigo bya Mugenyi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1300–1500</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Bigo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bigo bya Mugenyi is an archaeological site on the Katonga River in western Uganda, consisting of kilometres of deep ditches enclosing large areas of grassland. Dated to around the 14th and 15th centuries, it is thought to have protected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and settlements, and oral traditions link it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chwezi">Chwezi</a> rulers of Kitara. It is one of the largest earthwork sites in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>.</p></div>
